$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4efc9eae-928f-5278-9f56-8121eaff619e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z=2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260546} {:answer/id #uuid "56bcbb99-ce72-59cd-a9da-33457c9eeeea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z=2$ and $z=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260616} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c5bece-8709-5c6f-953e-b95c15e9a5c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z=-4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261330} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dff8cf-b0c0-51d5-9a81-f840b21c982a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z=-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261354} {:answer/id #uuid "f27bc899-6e84-544b-b720-a4da47800ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z=3$ and $z=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z=2$ and $z=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260616} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2ae1154-33c8-55c1-a139-f5a3593f1f5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262523}] :question/id #uuid "4a2306da-fb1e-5f54-9eaa-7c434b50af89" :question/math-academy-id "q-128116" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${r}_{33}$ is $3$, find all the possible values of $z$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}z & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & z-8 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6z\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}z & -3 & ∗ \\\\ -5 & z-8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${r}_{33}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}z & -3 \\\\ 5 & z-8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}z & -3 \\\\ 5 & z-8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =z\\cdot (z-8)-(-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-8z+15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${r}_{33}$ is $3$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-8z+15 & =3 \\\\ {z}^{2}-8z+12 & =0 \\\\ (z-2)(z-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=2$ and $z=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03da91b8-6945-5686-9351-3c4f2a121ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284819} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb19540-779a-5680-9b97-ccb80a7ac909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285045} {:answer/id #uuid "33d9982a-7134-5ad7-844e-bbc9746e0a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285265} {:answer/id #uuid "4e8d2a04-1b9b-59e4-9447-472af641f042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285518} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f7158f-08ab-5ab5-9b15-1b6ba9f274e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285265} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fe91b16-7bb5-5fee-825a-71898aec9fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287285}] :question/id #uuid "57a8c36e-10e7-5723-a51e-3f702886bc0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-18239" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${c}_{23}$ is $-86$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 11 & x & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 11 & x & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${c}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 7 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot x-7\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =-3x-77.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${c}_{23}$ is $-86$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x-77 & =-86 \\\\ -3x & =-9 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3099eaa6-4b6f-58d3-a20c-9e574800d61c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285228} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc690f8-8e07-55f4-8839-bcfd3ac6d35d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285528} {:answer/id #uuid "53b0a722-e98a-5141-a397-ceb56dfd3fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285558} {:answer/id #uuid "cefbccf2-76c7-528f-976c-2fc924b3b1ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286665} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a22ad1-ee4c-52e9-a3b2-e484761cb1db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285228} :answer-field/id #uuid "9439831c-5a0c-52e1-97f2-388e83df1619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287455}] :question/id #uuid "91242bf5-7032-5c91-b598-187db5bd0165" :question/math-academy-id "q-18240" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 9 & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & 1 & -5 \\\\ ∗ & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${d}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot x-11\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =x+55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+55 & =43 \\\\ x & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-12.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08742277-f22c-56fb-a39e-d1754f73d19e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284853} {:answer/id #uuid "341bc72b-cf1c-5b22-a308-8ca908245b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285267} {:answer/id #uuid "b1854847-c3b6-556b-a65f-b735e817e6fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=9$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286411} {:answer/id #uuid "c3fd8e0b-2c92-5f28-a313-e353447d0d87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-9$ and $x=9$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286585} {:answer/id #uuid "f1771426-3d54-57bf-af36-f5369502f74b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-9$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285267} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cc9940-acc7-5f8a-9164-f7d3768042c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287477}] :question/id #uuid "08ae3579-998d-5c2c-b385-d2da59a9828c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18243" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -{x}^{2} & -10 \\\\ -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -{x}^{2} & ∗ \\\\ -5 & 8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${b}_{33}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 8-(-5)\\cdot (-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =48-5{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}48-5{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ 45-5{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 9-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (3-x)(3+x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-3$ and $x=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b1c0f80-7e59-56d1-9cad-3841c5d78aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285028} {:answer/id #uuid "50fc9051-30fe-5e18-82d4-5dcaecf5f141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285533} {:answer/id #uuid "92520736-f07a-5196-b3fc-b28bb58f9775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286117} {:answer/id #uuid "9b4250d3-0fd2-5566-92bf-a2046949f6b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286210} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc98c46-73fe-5123-b4fa-233b6c24e079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286210} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2229c2d-6d32-5164-af94-112101e41325" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287545}] :question/id #uuid "90c16fd3-49c0-54c6-b69c-d1b74902f840" :question/math-academy-id "q-18247" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $-50$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ x & 1 & 3x \\\\ -12 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and second column:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ x & ∗ & 3x \\\\ ∗ & -4 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${a}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 \\\\ x & 3x\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 4 \\\\ x & 3x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-7)\\cdot 3x-x\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-21x-4x \\\\  & =-25x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $-50$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-25x & =-50 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0557d8f0-88df-5919-b3f5-641054f22058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290662} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d08694-26ed-5f00-a4b8-3a745de46f6b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291899}] :question/id #uuid "eece0e29-4499-5a90-9335-6884672ea4cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-275502" :question/problem "$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is $18$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${c}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is $18$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =18 \\\\ 6x & =30 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7fbb496-10c2-5fbe-b1cc-db506c593357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291430} :answer-field/id #uuid "5765fa5e-52ec-5827-8e07-3f8e94ea5e54" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fdd7f66a-09f9-54cd-8538-8ae68323acd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291713} :answer-field/id #uuid "57cee8c7-4a91-5107-b1fa-236b71c2ef79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292002}] :question/id #uuid "1e50a27f-78dc-5ec6-a61b-ce762c33947d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275530" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & p\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 4 \\\\ ∗ & -2 & p\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =p\\cdot p-4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}+8 & =17 \\\\ {p}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ (p-3)(p+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=-3$ and $p=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97cd2c38-264f-5fd7-86b9-15d8feb66f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298210} :answer-field/id #uuid "74343cf9-477d-534f-9fd9-9fdc02ec3695" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299032}] :question/id #uuid "e3151e3d-6c78-54a8-9112-7e12bf0e69ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-319129" :question/problem "$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}y & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $y$ in the matrix above.\n\n$y=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}y & ∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =y\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-2 & =10 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d0de1ec-1e6a-5a6c-8cd2-246cba1070d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297614} :answer-field/id #uuid "514ccbd8-214b-54f4-8036-636348dcb5e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298913}] :question/id #uuid "a1f4a024-dc0c-52c9-8ff4-2f9fe15cbc4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-319138" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =10 \\\\ 6x & =22 \\\\ x & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80d46a9c-4ef3-56cb-9cd4-3def1265ed25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298107} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7b88a1-b702-5fff-b93f-0fc50af656d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299319}] :question/id #uuid "810d97cb-2aa4-5e9c-adea-dac6f0944774" :question/math-academy-id "q-319139" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & r & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, find the value of $r$ in the matrix above.\n\n$r=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & r & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & r \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & =1\\cdot 8-r\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =8-7r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-7r & =15 \\\\ -7r & =7 \\\\ r & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $r=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8a63346-e03d-5825-b9fd-35bcc58cd5e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298428} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5fc495f-c169-5f09-9a4d-8bef0a7b185a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299415} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8b72332-11af-5580-8417-df0628d097e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298613} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3296d8f-9ada-57f3-b8c3-8775afed0112" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299454}] :question/id #uuid "c0ff50c0-0f9a-524e-8769-13e8da78335f" :question/math-academy-id "q-319146" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 7 \\\\ 6 & -8 & p-15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 7 \\\\ ∗ & -8 & p-15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =p(p-15)-7(-8) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}-15p+56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-15p+56 & =0 \\\\ (p-7)(p-8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=7$ and $p=8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4868dc7c-4591-51c4-8c0c-18cf96ef97c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=3$ and $k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327563} {:answer/id #uuid "56426e41-0ae2-51ef-90ee-44b9799a3014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=-3$ and $k=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327681} {:answer/id #uuid "92f690f5-6576-5167-8072-cb55e175e117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=8$ and $k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328215} {:answer/id #uuid "cdda320c-2f55-597a-919f-16872c2957b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328744} {:answer/id #uuid "da166514-b733-510c-bb0e-b10a765641d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=3$ and $k=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=3$ and $k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327563} :answer-field/id #uuid "51e89c8b-e506-5fea-9931-1f4c199251a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329334}] :question/id #uuid "9ddea2c0-c4c7-57d8-a6b1-8dfad87c989e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42614" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 9k-15 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ & 1 \\\\ ∗ & -4 & ∗ \\\\ 9k-15 & ∗ & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${m}_{22}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)-(9k-15)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6-(9k-15) \\\\  & =-9k+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9k+9 & =3{k}^{2}-45 \\\\ -3k+3 & ={k}^{2}-15 \\\\ {k}^{2}+3k-18 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=3$ and $k=-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b9eaaa1-9a11-5e97-894b-033fdcba3183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=-1$ and $k=-2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401690} {:answer/id #uuid "13957928-5c88-587e-8787-1039aba9a145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401691} {:answer/id #uuid "23eb6ae8-6643-5983-b5dd-d782a53c5d86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=-2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401692} {:answer/id #uuid "daaad303-eb94-54dc-b583-e74bb50bf666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=0$ and $k=-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401693} {:answer/id #uuid "01dc8965-c2ae-5ff0-b5e5-19a4d4675483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=10$ and $k=-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=-1$ and $k=-2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401690} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e6e33e7-dd66-569c-9ddd-b087772632c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401689}] :question/id #uuid "5a62d5fa-3b38-507f-b4fe-dfd19836563a" :question/math-academy-id "q-18244" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${a}_{22}$ is $-70$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2k & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 11 & 9 & k+3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2k & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 11 & ∗ & k+3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${a}_{22}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}2k & 6 \\\\ 11 & k+3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2k & 6 \\\\ 11 & k+3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2k\\cdot (k+3)-11\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k-66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{22}$ is $-70$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+6k-66 & =-70 \\\\ 2{k}^{2}+6k+4 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2}+3k+2 & =0 \\\\ (k+1)(k+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=-2.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :topic/math-academy-id 233 :topic/title "The Minors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176678} :activity/id #uuid "6410482c-1a4b-55b8-afc6-f009af1b05ff" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176643 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00cf6180-070b-5ebf-af24-bc4c4b0bd94e"} :step/id #uuid "c6666ad3-c461-5111-a9f4-d5a6f4f8e51a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176645}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176644 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175929 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0e83dcf-3ce6-5583-bd28-fdbc805a9403"} :step/id #uuid "3ddd6359-72c0-5eee-87d9-df029bef4a21" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176643}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176645 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad17d11-325f-5888-a5cd-61ee27f7a103"} :step/id #uuid "8cbda370-20f2-5e6b-9780-b0122e4ee2a0"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176975 :tutorial/content "Let's find the eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda=-\\textrm{i}$ of the matrix ![](images/a3/a351d711bda1d0b7009e0c2aa9ac8265e061e103f24dc2ff8c221711189a57e7.svg)\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =-\\textrm{i},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+\\text{i} & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}(1+\\text{i}){x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+(-1+\\text{i}){x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, since the matrix $A-(-\\textrm{i})I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another.\n\nAs a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables as the free variable. For example, from the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2 = (1+\\textrm{i})x_1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by setting $x_1\\in\\mathbb C$ to be the free variable, we find that the general solution to our system is given by\n\n![](images/8e/8eef5a23053809341f427e7099c364d65fa24d8144e4feac2a9d817accaa5a88.svg)\n\nSetting $x_1=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n![](images/40/40c4333ba45ec2afa3479f682fcba72c2b61d69c4a4611b30b0d4078731e0a8b.svg)\n\nNotice that our eigenvector has complex-valued entries.\n\n**Note:** To check our result, we can show that $A\\mathbf v = \\lambda \\mathbf v.$ Computing $A\\mathbf v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand computing $\\lambda \\mathbf v$ gives\n\n![](images/12/12fed2087f821e6e5da14d844b61e8300c8a4dc98ac4eff96f719fcc5795b5b4.svg)\n\nSo $A\\mathbf v = \\lambda \\mathbf v,$ as required." :tutorial/id #uuid "1bde3a85-d8df-5194-8581-77fe2108627c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4297 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "8f4ddd6c-a17e-54f3-bade-a64685e04b36" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176644}}] :activity/title "Finding Complex Eigenvectors of Real 2x2 Matrices" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186176123} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411587} :activity/id #uuid "3099b967-b00c-5782-9a83-fd84f9ad579c" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411585 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351252 :question/id #uuid "fbfe9a5f-3d3d-54aa-9e82-2b9e587c84ba"} :step/id #uuid "42de2582-1d6d-5484-ba6c-324ba0f7ff5f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411586}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411586 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375432 :question/id #uuid "0ee811a8-c053-59bb-b00f-f224606c0564"} :step/id #uuid "741564cd-c2f1-5aee-8b62-848c21e617d3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411588}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411587 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411584 :question/id #uuid "db7154e6-6fda-5907-98f7-b3398371be54"} :step/id #uuid "7c22f243-0739-5a0f-8281-eeed84387bab" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411589}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411588 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272077 :question/id #uuid "8845c35f-ffc0-56f1-b7af-e5bdef685e2b"} :step/id #uuid "d4502c0c-e4ff-5fb4-9162-5b78360320c6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411589 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326744 :question/id #uuid "0ea0f7da-291a-5ef5-afec-bc983b4386ad"} :step/id #uuid "db758ac7-852d-51b4-ad30-e5acef4cfcd0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411585}}] :activity/title "Finding Complex Eigenvectors of Real 2x2 Matrices" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411577} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475991} :activity/id #uuid "9c7a70fd-abbe-516b-95be-41d0d36b0d99" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475991 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326747 :question/id #uuid "cb7ad820-361f-5675-a375-d91857e5a50d"} :step/id #uuid "4638cfef-2e48-5d74-ab48-bf41cd68013c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218