0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69bcd314-df9c-5935-9335-a09fa25e8d41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472592} {:answer/id #uuid "8865af33-97aa-5c4a-9244-e60cc4cee987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472592} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c83300b-74eb-54e0-bc36-0514d541679a" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38fb9531-056d-5ceb-831d-52b028bb8fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218647259