0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${a}_{43}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db004ed2-ed81-5217-88ac-e52284d7ad3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473296} {:answer/id #uuid "002f6cc8-519c-547f-b765-dd76618c0b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473296} :answer-field/id #uuid "f127a0d3-e90a-58f9-8f2b-6e15c5df7965" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db