*bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c544f2-0094-5efb-b9d7-430a6628b03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473118} {:answer/id #uuid "d6421a79-149e-5798-8b1f-119bfea53fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fafc7937-f74b-546b-b87e-a22ca804ac3f" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a89bbf83-2e3e-5555-a6d5-981a9278f764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473120} {:answer/id #uuid "cea56d01-fdfe-5736-816e-b8204e960080" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473120} :answer-field/id #uuid "8372ee30-4548-5d83-9957-bf0d65799b1f" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc580dff-bc2e-5878-b7a7-f48a863b4636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473122} {:answer/id #uuid "2be2d645-5052-599b-a84f-9d2d9883a16a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473123} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d08e1cd-2808-5a00-b091-ce22e53c0263" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473956}] :question/id #uuid "72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42005" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128927 :question/id #uuid "97237f8e-b317-5c86-86d1-8fd3cc83e66b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4689" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A  &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{4} & 7 & 8 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{red}-1}} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{6} & 5 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{red}1}} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{red}2}} & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &\\longrightarrow \\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{4} & 7 & 8 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{6} & 5 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{4}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525160 :question-generator/id #uuid "3df9683d-9911-5e33-b527-b010d4561f83" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186129115.py"} :knowledg